.TH RATTSPEC 1 "2026-10-05" "Rattpack 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rattspec \- create or update Rattpack specifications through an AI backend, and
map directories into a terse inventory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rattspec assist
.I REQUEST
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B rattspec map
.I DIRECTORY
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B rattspec
.RB { --opencode | --openai }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rattspec assist
creates or updates the root
.B Rattspec
and
.B Rattpkg
files from a natural-language request. Quote REQUEST when it contains spaces or
shell metacharacters. Select a backend with
.B \-\-opencode
or
.BR \-\-openai ;
without either, the backend comes from the configuration file.
.PP
The command reads existing root files, plus a terse directory map when one has
been cached, and sends them to the selected backend. It accepts complete
replacement files in a JSON proposal. Unchanged files can be omitted; missing
root files must be created.
.PP
Before writing, the whole proposal must parse and lint, declare exactly one
project/package identity, and include at least one target in Rattspec. The real
package manifest reader validates dependency sources, pins, and checksums.
Generated Rattscript is never evaluated. Files are published atomically only if
their existing contents still match the initial read.
.PP
The command does not resolve dependencies or write Rattpkg.lock. Follow-up steps
may appear in the generated summary.
.PP
.B rattspec map
scans a directory and writes a compact binary map to
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/rattpack/<directoryname>.bin .
The same map is attached to assist requests, so a large project is described by
one short inventory instead of a long path list. With
.B \-\-print
the map is also written as the terse text described in MAP DSL below.
.SH BACKENDS
.TP
.B \-\-opencode
Use OpenCode V2 through the
.B opencode api
command, which applies that CLI's service discovery and authentication. The
request is issued with
.B \-\-standalone
so it never waits on or is redirected by the shared background service. Pass
.B \-\-no\-standalone
to share the service instead.
.TP
.B \-\-openai
Use any server speaking the OpenAI API, via the vendored openaipp client.
Credentials may be a bearer API key or HTTP basic user and password; when a user
is given it takes precedence over the key. Both
.B /chat/completions
and
.B /responses
are supported.
.PP
The two flags are mutually exclusive.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-C " DIRECTORY" ", \--directory=" DIRECTORY
Project directory for
.BR assist ,
and the default directory for
.BR map .
Default: current directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-plugin= PATH
Assist plugin library. Default: the backend's plugin, named
.B opencode-assist
or
.BR openai-assist ,
in
.I plugins/
beside the rattspec executable, with the platform's shared-library suffix.
The plugin must match the host's D compiler family/major and shared runtime.
.TP
.BI \-\-opencode\-executable= EXECUTABLE
OpenCode executable name or path. Default: opencode, found using PATH.
.TP
.BI \-\-server= URL
Explicit OpenCode server. By default, use the CLI's discovery and
authentication.
.TP
.BR \-\-standalone ", " \-\-no\-standalone
Run OpenCode with a private server. Default: enabled.
.TP
.BI \-\-openai\-url= URL
OpenAI-compatible base URL, including any path prefix such as
.IR /v1 .
.TP
.BI \-\-openai\-key= KEY
OpenAI bearer API key.
.TP
.BI \-\-openai\-user= USER
OpenAI basic-auth user. Takes precedence over the API key.
.TP
.BI \-\-openai\-password= PASSWORD
OpenAI basic-auth password.
.TP
.BI \-\-openai\-api= NAME
OpenAI endpoint family:
.B chat
for /chat/completions or
.B responses
for /responses. Default: chat.
.TP
.BI \-\-model= MODEL
For OpenCode,
.I provider/model
or
.IR provider/model#variant .
For OpenAI, the model name. Defaults to the configured model, or OpenCode's own
default.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout= SECONDS
Request deadline. Default: 120 seconds. Must be a positive integer no larger
than 2147483647.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
With
.BR assist ,
generate and validate the proposal, print it as JSON, and write no files. The
request still runs.
.TP
.BI \-\-map\-out= PATH
With
.BR map ,
write the binary map to PATH instead of the cache directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-summary ", " \-\-no\-summary
With
.BR map ,
include directory file and byte totals in the rendered text. Default: enabled.
.TP
.B \-\-print
With
.BR map ,
print the rendered map text after writing the binary map.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display the version and exit.
.PP
Boolean long options accept negative spellings such as \--no\-dry-run.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Tooling settings are read from
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rattpack/Rattpack.json
on POSIX and
.IR %APPDATA% / rattpack / Rattpack.json
on Windows. The file is optional and independent of
.IR Config.toml ,
which is build configuration read by Rattscript. Every value may be overridden
by an environment variable or a command-line flag.
.PP
Values are resolved as: command-line flag, then environment, then this file,
then the built-in default.
.TP
.B backend
.B opencode
or
.BR openai .
.TP
.B opencode.executable
, .B opencode.server
, .B opencode.model
, .B opencode.timeout
, .B opencode.standalone
.TP
.B openai.base_url
, .B openai.api_key
, .B openai.user
, .B openai.password
, .B openai.organization
, .B openai.project
, .B openai.model
, .B openai.api
, .B openai.timeout
.TP
.B map.summary
, .B map.max_entries
.TP
.B plugins
, .B scripts
, .B commands
Objects of name to string, overriding plugin library paths and naming script
and command locations for tooling.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.EX
{
  "backend": "openai",
  "openai": {
    "base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1",
    "user": "builder",
    "password": "secret",
    "model": "local-model",
    "api": "chat"
  },
  "opencode": { "standalone": true },
  "map": { "summary": true, "max_entries": 200000 },
  "scripts": { "scaffold": "tools/scaffold.ratt" },
  "commands": { "format": "clang-format" }
}
.EE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR OPENAI_BASE ", " OPENAI_API_BASE
OpenAI-compatible base URL.
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
OpenAI bearer API key.
.TP
.BR OPENAI_USER ", " RATTPACK_OPENAI_USER
OpenAI basic-auth user.
.TP
.BR OPENAI_PASSWORD ", " RATTPACK_OPENAI_PASSWORD
OpenAI basic-auth password.
.TP
.BR OPENAI_ORG_ID ", " OPENAI_PROJECT_ID
Optional OpenAI organization and project headers.
.TP
.BR OPENAI_MODEL ", " RATTPACK_OPENAI_MODEL
OpenAI model name.
.TP
.B RATTPACK_OPENAI_API
OpenAI endpoint family, chat or responses.
.TP
.B RATTPACK_OPENAI_TIMEOUT
OpenAI request deadline in seconds.
.TP
.B RATTPACK_OPENAI_URL, RATTPACK_OPENAI_KEY
Alternative spellings of the OpenAI URL and key.
.TP
.BR OPENCODE ", " RATTPACK_OPENCODE
OpenCode executable name or path.
.TP
.B RATTPACK_OPENCODE_SERVER
Explicit OpenCode server URL.
.TP
.BR RATTPACK_OPENCODE_MODEL ", " OPENCODE_MODEL
OpenCode model selection.
.TP
.B RATTPACK_OPENCODE_STANDALONE
Set to 0, false, no, or off to share the background service.
.TP
.B RATTPACK_OPENCODE_TIMEOUT
OpenCode request deadline in seconds.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " APPDATA
Location of the Rattpack configuration directory.
.TP
.BR XDG_CACHE_HOME ", " LOCALAPPDATA
Location of the directory map cache.
.TP
.B PATH
Search path for the default OpenCode executable.
.SH MAP DSL
The text form of a directory map is one entry per line, indented by one space
per depth level. A colon separates a name from its attributes. Inside a name, a
backslash escapes a backslash, a colon, or a space.
.PP
.EX
d NAME:F COUNT:B BYTES   directory, with total files and bytes below it
f NAME:X:BYTES:HASH      file; X marks an executable
l NAME                   symbolic link
x NAME                   any other entry kind
.EE
.PP
COUNT is a plain integer. BYTES uses k and M suffixes. HASH is eight lowercase
hex digits of the file's content fingerprint, and is present only for source and
build-input file types. For example:
.PP
.EX
d demo:F6:B273.5k
 f README.md:7:b21109ab
 f run.sh:X:10:bc1f407a
 d src:F4:B273.5k
  f main.c:22:0b377551
  d core:F2:B28
   f util.c:19:f86d8b1f
.EE
.PP
Version-control metadata, build output directories, dependency caches, and dot
entries are never mapped. Entries are sorted, so the same tree always renders
identically.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Rattspec
Root project identity and build targets.
.TP
.I Rattpkg
Root package identity and dependencies.
.TP
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/rattpack/*.bin
Binary directory maps, one per mapped directory.
.TP
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rattpack/Rattpack.json
Optional tooling configuration.
.TP
.I PREFIX/bin/plugins/opencode\-assist.so
Default plugin location on POSIX. macOS uses .dylib and Windows uses .dll.
Install the plugins using install.sh \--with\-plugins, or select \--plugin.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success, help, or version output; 1 indicates an application
diagnostic or assist failure; 2 indicates argument parsing failure.
Diagnostics go to standard error. E_ASSIST reports failed, timed-out, or
unusable backend responses and concurrent edits; E_MAP reports a directory or
map file that cannot be read; E_PLUGIN_ABI reports plugin failures.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rattspec map . --print
rattspec assist 'add these libraries: fmt and zlib' --opencode
rattspec assist 'build a C library and an executable that links it' \-\-openai \\
    \-\-openai\-url http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1 \-\-openai\-user builder \-\-model my\-model
rattspec map src \-\-map\-out /tmp/src.bin
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
